paw is a dotfiles manager for Linux, macOS, and WSL.

Usage:
  paw [flags]
  paw [command]

Available Commands:
  audit             Audit repository structure and completeness
  backup            Backup management
  completion        Generate shell completions
  doctor            Health check and diagnostics
  help              Help about any command
  init              Clone dotfiles repo and configure paw
  install           Install packages and create symlinks
  link              Create symlinks only
  man               Generate man pages
  migrate-ts-config Migrate dotfiles.config.ts to paw.toml
  push              Commit and push dotfiles changes
  rollback          Restore backups and remove links from last run
  scaffold          Generate missing config templates
  status            Show current symlink and package state
  sync              Pull repo and refresh links
  unlink            Remove managed symlinks
  update            Self-update paw binary

Flags:
      --auto-update         Auto update during sync
  -n, --dry-run             Show what would be done
  -f, --force               Overwrite existing files
  -h, --help                help for paw
      --json                JSON output mode
      --log-format string   Log format: text|json (default "text")
      --no-interactive      Disable interactive prompts
  -p, --path string         Path used by init command
  -q, --quiet               Quiet output
      --skip-hooks          Skip lifecycle hooks
      --skip-packages       Skip package installation
      --skip-update         Skip update check
      --skip-verify         Skip attestation verification in update
  -v, --verbose             Verbose output
      --version             version for paw

Use "paw [command] --help" for more information about a command.
